We will start with **direct substitution** (step A):

$\begin{align}
f(\blueD {6})&=\dfrac{(\blueD {6})^2-10(\blueD {6})+24}{(\blueD {6})^2-4(\blueD {6})-12}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{36-60+24}{36-24-12}
\\\\
&=\dfrac00
\end{align}$

We got the **indeterminate form** $\dfrac00$ (step D).

Now we need to determine which analytical method is applicable.

Since we have a quotient with polynomial expressions, we will use the method of **factoring** (step E):

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{x^2-10x+24}{x^2-4x-12}&=\dfrac{\cancel{(x-6)}(x-4)}{\cancel{(x-6)}(x+2)}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{x-4}{x+2}
\end{align}$

Now we can try **direct substitution** (step A) once again!

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{(\blueD{6})-4}{(\blueD{6})+2}&=\dfrac{2}{8}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{4}
\end{align}$

We got a number, so we've **found the limit** (step C)!

This means $\displaystyle\lim_{x\to 6}f(x)=\dfrac{1}{4}$.
